<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no trade - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no trade - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Inquiry and demand was fair. Sales confirmed for the week on 146,500 head (record weekly volume) including 31,700 head or about 22 percent previously contracted or formulated cattle. Bids 63.00 with extra days, asking 64.00- 65.00. Last sales 63.00 Thursday. Sales FOB feedlot net weights after 4 percent shrink.</p>
<p>Confirmed - none</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
